I kept the “one query” goal, but I did not load all contacts in the org into memory. With roughly 2.3 million contacts, a synchronous `SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry FROM Contact` can blow past Apex query-row, heap, and CPU limits, and can make a 200-account MDM batch fail. Instead, the handler performs a single bulk query scoped only to the accounts whose `BillingCountry` changed and only to contacts that could possibly qualify (`blank` or matching a previous country). If a single changed account can have more than 50,000 qualifying contacts or more than 10,000 records to update, this still needs to move to asynchronous Batch/Queueable processing, but the synchronous handler below is the safe production pattern for normal volumes.

